**Step 4: Add JavaScript to create the tooltip**

Create a JavaScript function to create the tooltip element and display it when the user hovers over the SVG. We'll also add an event listener to remove the tooltip when the user stops hovering over the SVG.

```javascript
const tooltip = document.getElementById('tooltip');

document.getElementById('svg-container').addEventListener('mouseover', () => {
  const svgRect = document.getElementById('svg-container').getBoundingClientRect();
  const x = svgRect.left + svgRect.width / 2;
  const y = svgRect.top + svgRect.height / 2;

  tooltip.style.left = `${x}px`;
  tooltip.style.top = `${y}px`;
  tooltip.style.visibility = 'visible';
});

document.getElementById('svg-container').addEventListener('mouseout', () => {
  tooltip.style.visibility = 'hidden';
});
```

